Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 13:53:03 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] =?UTF-8?q?quic:=20annotate=20quic=5Fbacklog=5Frcv()?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20too=20=E2=80=94=20cover=20the=20lock-contended=20backlog-dra?=
 =?UTF-8?q?in=20path?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The softirq fast-path annotation in quic_packet_rcv() brackets only the direct
sk_backlog_rcv() dispatch (socket not busy). When the sock lock is held the packet
is queued via sk_add_backlog() and drained later from release_sock() ->
quic_backlog_rcv() in process context, which the fast-path bracket does not cover
(reported by Xin Long). Bracket quic_packet_process() in quic_backlog_rcv() on the
same connection kcov handle so lock-contended packets are attributed too.
---
 net/quic/socket.c | 15 ++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/net/quic/socket.c b/net/quic/socket.c
index 09cc48f89df8c..c5bdf96ebf9b3 100644
--- a/net/quic/socket.c
+++ b/net/quic/socket.c
@@ -2903,7 +2903,20 @@ static void quic_shutdown(struct sock *sk, int how)
 
 static int quic_backlog_rcv(struct sock *sk, struct sk_buff *skb)
 {
-	return quic_packet_process(sk, skb, GFP_ATOMIC);
+	int ret;
+
+	/* Backlog-drain path: the socket was busy (lock held) when the packet
+	 * arrived, so quic_packet_rcv() queued it with sk_add_backlog() and it
+	 * is processed here from release_sock() in process context. The softirq
+	 * fast-path annotation in quic_packet_rcv() does NOT bracket this path
+	 * (reported by Xin Long), so lock-contended packets would miss remote
+	 * kcov attribution. Bracket the same quic_packet_process() dispatch here
+	 * on the connection's kcov handle; a no-op when the handle is zero.
+	 */
+	quic_kcov_remote_start(quic_sk(sk)->kcov_handle);
+	ret = quic_packet_process(sk, skb, GFP_ATOMIC);
+	quic_kcov_remote_stop();
+	return ret;
 }
 
 struct proto quic_prot = {
